# VALORA / VANTAGE Development Guide

## Prerequisites

- Docker Desktop installed and running
- Git

## Get the project

```powershell
git clone "https://github.com/dillan-garahushoma/Vantage.git"
cd Vantage
```

If you already have a clone, use `git pull` on the branch you intend to work from.

## Start the current backend stack

The checked-in Docker Compose stack currently supports PostgreSQL and the FastAPI API. The React frontend is not yet checked into this repository, so do not expect the `valora_frontend` service or `http://localhost:4173` to be available.

```powershell
docker compose -f backend/docker-compose.yml up -d --build db api
```

You should see these containers:

- `valora_db`
- `valora_api`

## API endpoints

- API: `http://localhost:8000`
- OpenAPI documentation: `http://localhost:8000/docs`
- Health check: `http://localhost:8000/health`

## Database migrations

Run migrations from the backend directory after PostgreSQL is available:

```powershell
cd backend
.\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic -c alembic.ini upgrade head
```

## Current delivery status

The VALORA operational foundation is in active development. Estate tenancy, resident-only signup, estate authorization, complaint lifecycle history, and provider-authorized work orders are implemented. Security incidents, deterministic Living Score v1, seed data, frontend, and final end-to-end validation are still in progress.

See `tasks/todo.md` and the documents in `docs/` for the current implementation plan and product specification.
